<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AnalysisLevel>preview</AnalysisLevel>
    <AnalysisMode>AllEnabledByDefault</AnalysisMode>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Promptuarium</PackageId>
    <Title>Promptuarium</Title>
    <Description>Promptuarium is a versatile, tree-based data structure to store or exchange data and metadata efficiently (in binary format). Written in pure C#, can be used in F#, too.</Description>
    <PackageTags>promptuarium binary tree serialization space-efficient limitless container</PackageTags>
    <ReleaseNotes>New: Promptuarium.Serializer, a separate, experimental package (opt-in PRMTSER000): .NET objects to trees and back, without JSON, in the layout of SERIALIZER_FORMAT.md (PRMT:GEN1-LE, PRMT:CFG1-LE or a signature of the application), with comments. pedit and PStudio show the metadata before the data. PStudio: only the forms that give a content back byte for byte are offered; the tags and the type codes of the serializer layout by name; the chosen forms are remembered for every file (View / Reset Types forgets them); File / Open Recent; the settings are kept. GetStatistics().ToString() lists the metadata lines first. The library API and the binary format are unchanged.</ReleaseNotes>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>YAML is the preferred text format of the tools (YamlDotNet, used by the tools only). pcfg export writes YAML by default, with the comments as # lines and a BLOB as !!binary, and pcfg import reads it back (YAML 1.2 core schema; aliases and several documents are refused). Breaking for scripts: pcfg export without options no longer writes JSON; JSON is written with --json or into a .json file, and a .json file or --json is still imported as JSON, e.g. appsettings.json. New: pcfg get --yaml, the yaml:YAML form of pcfg set, and --yaml in pedit (dump, chunks, add, set, delete), next to --json; the text output of pedit is unchanged. Breaking for scripts: pedit dump --json is a tree now, the children nested in their parents, instead of a flat list with depths; empty contents and children are left out, and truncated appears only if --max-bytes shortened a content. New: pedit add and set --tree take a whole subtree, in the form of dump --yaml or dump --json, from a file or the standard input. The library, its API and the binary format are unchanged since 8.1.0.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
